{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe LLM gates carry leftovers from finished cutovers and one retired demo: the single-pass review-a-ticket engine (a demo the project has been retiring; the real reviews are the four-phase plan review and four-phase code review, whose single-turn criteria are steps inside those workflows), two shadow comparators, a spot-eval harness with an unreachable entry point, private re-exports that ADR 0111 forbids, severity residue from ADR 0108, a finished A/B env var, a legacy overlay routing form that clients may still use, and five attestation helpers independently confirmed dead on origin/main. Each is small; together they are the kind of retained rollback twin the operator named as the target class on 2026-09-06.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The single-pass demo is fully retired: its engine, parity harness, prompt, eval spec, and eval-solver branch are gone, the catalog has exactly one default reviewer (`code-quality`), and the four-phase plan-review and code-review workflows are byte-unchanged. **The default flag must be flipped explicitly, not inherited.** `ticket_quality.md` is today the ONLY front-matter `default: true`; every other reviewer — `code_quality.md` included — is `default: false`. `index.json` is generated from that front-matter, and `operations.default_reviewer_id()` returns the first entry whose `default` is set, otherwise raising `LLMError(\"no default reviewer is configured in the catalog\")`. So deleting the demo WITHOUT setting `default: true` in `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code_quality.md` and regenerating leaves ZERO defaults and breaks every caller that selects a reviewer. The demo story owns both edits in one change. Checked by the demo story's greps, the regenerate-index drift gate, and a test asserting `default_reviewer_id() == \"code-quality\"`.\n- [ ] No finished-cutover scaffolding remains: the shadow comparators, the spot-eval harness, and the private re-exports are deleted with their only importers migrated. Checked by the scaffolding story's greps.\n- [ ] Severity no longer drives any gate policy, `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` is gone with prefetch always on, and the legacy overlay `activate:` list form warns once per overlay through the deprecation registry while still working. Checked by the priority-driven step tests, the prefetch spy test, and the two overlay warning tests.\n- [ ] The five dead attestation helpers are removed, the duplicated unresolvable-ref message is single-sourced, and the plan-review status surface emits only values its schema declares. Checked by the attestation story's greps and the parametrized status test.\n- [ ] Every client-facing change carries a release-notes line. Checked by the entries each story adds.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- Cutover scaffolding story: delivers criterion 2.\n- Demo retirement story: delivers criterion 1, depends on the scaffolding story (shared test file and a relocated-prompts tuple). It carries the `code_quality.md` front-matter flip + index regeneration described in criterion 1.\n- Severity and prefetch story: delivers the severity and prefetch half of criterion 3.\n- Overlay warning story: delivers the overlay half of criterion 3, depends on the demo story for a registry note.\n- Attestation helpers story: delivers criterion 4.\n- Criterion 5 is delivered by each story's own release-notes line."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793150814225256830,"uuid":"6456247e-73cc-4bee-a104-3eec778ff440"}